      "content": "An INR (International Normalized Ratio) level of 4.2 is indeed higher than the normal range of 2.0-3.0, which indicates an increased risk of bleeding. Warfarin is a blood thinner that works by preventing the blood from clotting, so a high INR can lead to excessive bleeding or bruising. While eating more greens or taking vitamins may not significantly lower your INR, maintaining good health through a balanced diet can help support your overall blood health. It's still recommended to consult your doctor as they may need to adjust your dosage or monitor your INR more closely to ensure your safety.",
